 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Decide whether the two stages in these experiments are dependent or independent.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 515760,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You’re getting dressed to go to a party, and you plan to wear a blouse and a skirt. You choose the blouse first, then the skirt (assume that you’d be comfortable wearing any of your skirts with any of your blouses).",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Independent stages do not affect each other. Dependent stages do affect each other.</p>\n<p>If you do not care which colors go together, the choices of blouse and skirt are independent.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Independent"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 515761,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "On further reflection, you realize that some of your skirts clash with some of your blouses. So, you choose the blouse first, and then choose a skirt that goes with your chosen blouse. ",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Independent stages do not affect each other. Dependent stages do affect each other.</p>\n<p>Once you decide that if you choose the blue shirt, you will not wear the orange skirt (or something like that), the choices of blouse and skirt are dependent.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Dependent"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
